<%- include('partials/head') %>
  <body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

    <main>
      <h2>Open Source You Already Use</h2>

      <p>
        You probably use open source every day without knowing it. Here are a few I
        use.
      </p>

      <div class="two-col">
        <article>
          <img src="/img/brave.png" alt="Brave lion logo">
          <h3>Brave</h3>
          <p>
            The browser I use every day. It's built on Chromium, the open source base
            behind Chrome, and it blocks ads and trackers by default. Its own code is
            public on GitHub too.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <img src="/img/vlc.png" alt="VLC traffic cone logo">
          <h3>VLC</h3>
          <p>
            The media player that opens almost any video file you throw at it. It's
            made by volunteers and has never charged a cent.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <img src="/img/ollama.png" class="light-logo" alt="Ollama llama logo">
          <h3>Ollama</h3>
          <p>
            Lets you run AI chat models on your own laptop. It's free, there's no
            account, and nothing you type gets sent to a company's servers.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <img src="/img/vscode.png" alt="VS Code logo">
          <h3>VS Code</h3>
          <p>
            The editor I write my code in. Microsoft publishes the code behind it on
            GitHub, and thousands of people have helped improve it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <article class="live">
        <h3>Live from GitHub</h3>
        <p>
          Stars are like bookmarks, and forks are copies people made to work on.
          These numbers are pulled from GitHub, so they stay up to date.
        </p>
        <% if (projects.length == 0) { %>
          <p>GitHub isn't answering right now. Try again in a minute.</p>
        <% } else { %>
          <table>
            <tr>
              <th>Project</th>
              <th>Stars</th>
              <th>Forks</th>
              <th>License</th>
            </tr>
            <% for (let project of projects) { %>
              <tr>
                <td><a href="<%= project.html_url %>"><%= project.full_name %></a></td>
                <td><%= project.stargazers_count.toLocaleString() %></td>
                <td><%= project.forks_count.toLocaleString() %></td>
                <td><%= project.license ? project.license.spdx_id : "None" %></td>
              </tr>
            <% } %>
          </table>
          <p>Not sure what those licenses mean? Check the <a href="/licenses">Licenses</a> page.</p>
        <% } %>
      </article>

      <section class="sources">
        <h3>Sources</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Each project's code: <a href="https://github.com/brave/brave-browser">Brave</a>, <a href="https://www.videolan.org/vlc/">VLC</a>, <a href="https://github.com/ollama/ollama">Ollama</a>, <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/vscode">VS Code</a></li>
          <li>Logos from <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/">Wikimedia Commons</a></li>
          <li>Live numbers from the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/rest/search/search">GitHub REST API</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
  </body>
</html>
